From 49d0c2ae8016a3507d56d333e3297441723ecc59 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 09:20:15 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] reaper: one factory state, main network created by the setup
 box, dual-WAN shell pill

- Factory reset: restore_defaults_wifi() no longer applies the printed-label
  key (rc_support "defpsk" + wifi_psk). Label units reset to psk2 + the label
  key + w_Setting=1 while the rest reset open, so the first-boot banner judged
  them apart (GT-BE98_ICP field report). Every unit now resets to admin/admin
  and the open template Wi-Fi. rc_support "defpsk" itself is kept
  (firewall.c, ntpclient.c read it).
- Banner: reaper_wifi_default() also treats a key equal to wifi_psk as the
  factory key (backstop for the above).
- Setup box: the main network (MAINFH sdn_rl row + apm profile) is built only
  at boot by the closed init_apg() -> check_mwl_convert(), and only once
  x_Setting=1. The v3.2.9 reconcile (sync_apgx_to_wlunit + restart_sdn) only
  syncs existing rows and could not create it. The CGI now sets x_Setting=1
  and the page chain is saveNvram;restart_chpass;reboot; the done message
  says the router is restarting.
- Network page (SDN.asp): with no main network in router/AP mode, a notice
  links to the setup box.
- Banner strings: factory Wi-Fi is open, not "admin" (RSEC_5/9/13).
- Dual WAN: the shell WAN pill follows wan_primary (load-balance: either line
  up), as the dashboard already did; it read wan0 only.
- Tokens: RSEC_5/9/13 and RWFS_11 reworded, RSDN_1 new; 25 packs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
